-- title:
--   Regularity at ∞-branch cusp centres of X_H(q²M'), q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ for which some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ obtained as the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H(q^2M')$, where $H$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$, with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal, and with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$; let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the classical series $\mathsf q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{num}}$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f\cdot y=x$ in $L((\mathsf q))$. Write $B$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. The assertion is: for every prime ideal $y$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$, containing $j^{-1}$, and containing every $b\in B$ whose image in $K$ is a non-unit of $W_0$, and for every commutative ring $B_m$ that is an $B$-algebra realising the localisation of $B$ at $y$, the ring $B_m$ is a regular local ring and so is $B_m/(\varpi)$.
--
--   This is the cusp-regularity statement for the two-chart integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ at the centres lying on the $\infty$-branch cut out by the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$, in the case $q=2$: the pole chart is regular there and its special fibre over the residue characteristic of $A$ is regular as well. It feeds the statement that the two-chart model is regular with regular special fibre away from the image of the finite chart, on the Igusa leg of the semistable-covering argument.
